      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-5515",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/10/100ad4ead1a2a1b24ad74e830611c48c5478746caac4f027aa125ec7be314660.png)\n\nA square with sides of length $1.5$ is contained within a circle with a radius of $2$. A dart is aimed at the circle. Assuming that the dart lands on a random position inside the circle, what is the probability of the dart hitting the square? Round your answer to three decimal places.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
