      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-5518",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/fc/fc58b40cb253515b506c84ce88f3fc2373faced9cb8051fdc051e8a726e55f03.png)\n\nAn equilateral triangle that has sides of length $6$ and a height of length $3\\sqrt{3}$, contains a circle of radius of $1.5$. A dart is aimed at the triangle. Assuming that the dart lands on a random position inside the triangle, what is the probability of the dart hitting the circle? Round your answer to three decimal places.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
